cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "kinextract: Non-parametric binned-LOSVD spectral fitter for galaxy kinematics"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Waters
    given-names: Thomas, K.
    affiliation: University of Michigan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-05"
url: "https://github.com/thomas-k-waters/kinextract"
abstract: >
  kinextract fits galaxy spectra using a non-parametric line-of-sight velocity
  distribution (LOSVD) represented directly on a velocity grid, for any
  number of template spectra in a single fitting engine. Regularization
  strength is selected automatically via a bootstrap-estimated generalized
  AIC criterion. An optional shared multiplicative continuum can be
  co-fitted alongside the LOSVD and template weights. Uncertainty is
  quantified via a Laplace/curvature-approximation engine (validated across
  a broad sigma range via a production-scale coverage sweep) or parametric
  bootstrap, with an optional NUTS/NumPyro reference mode for
  simulation-based-calibration checks. The package targets
  integral-field-spectroscopy data (MUSE, STIS) for black-hole mass
  measurements through Schwarzschild orbit modelling.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - spectroscopy
  - galaxy kinematics
  - LOSVD
  - Schwarzschild orbit library modelling
license: MIT
